From {{derived|en|enm|*grapplen||to seize, lay hold of}}, from {{derived|en|ang|*græpplian||to seize}} (compare {{cog|ang|ġegræppian||to seize}}), from {{derived|en|gem-pro|*graipilōną}}, {{m|gem-pro|*grabbalōną||to seize}}, from {{derived|en|ine-pro|*gʰrebʰ-|t=to take, seize, rake}}, equivalent to {{suffix|en|grab|le}}.

Cognate with {{cog|nl|grabbelen||to grope, scramble, scrabble}}, {{cog|de|grabbeln||to rummage, grope about}} and {{m|de|grapsen}}, {{m|de|grapschen||to seize, grasp, grabble}}. Influenced in some senses by {{m|en|grapple||tool with claws or hooks|pos=noun}} (see below). See further at ''{{l|en|grasp}}''.

